   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The functions \\( f \\) and \\( g \\) are differentiable, with \\( f(3) = -4 \\), \\( f'(3) = 4 \\), \\( g(3) = -3 \\), \\( g'(3) = 7 \\). Let \\( h(x) = \\frac{f(x)}{g(x)} \\). Find the value of \\( h'(3) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         16,
         9
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Record the values at \\( x = 3 \\): \\( f(3) = -4 \\), \\( f'(3) = 4 \\), \\( g(3) = -3 \\), \\( g'(3) = 7 \\).",
         "mathjson": 4
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the quotient rule, \\( \\left(\\frac{f}{g}\\right)'(3) = \\frac{f'(3)g(3) - f(3)g'(3)}{[g(3)]^{2}} \\).",
         "mathjson": -4
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Substitute: \\( \\frac{(4)(-3) - (-4)(7)}{(-3)^{2}} = \\frac{16}{9} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            16,
            9
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( h'(3) = \\frac{16}{9} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            16,
            9
         ]
      }
   ],
